WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.260
CITY A – HERO ASSOCIATION HQ

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.720
Then it is decided that Mumen Rider

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.320
will remain the top-ranked class C hero.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.650
Understood. I will let him know.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.010
I simply cannot understand

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.230
why he has no desire
to move up to class B...

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:24.270
Our next agenda item is
the 55th Hero Certification Exam.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.610
For this exam,
the total number of candidates is...

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:31.250
11,684, with the exam offered
at six different venues.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.990
That is an increase of more than
22% over the previous exam.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.650
We mustn't be happy
with simple quantity.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.470
Even with more candidates,

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.960
if the quality of the heroes
is reduced,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.130
the numbers are meaningless.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:52.340
Therefore, we ought to be even more
critical during evaluations.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.100
Also, I hear that
a certain person of interest

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.560
is taking the exam this time.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.310
Yes, it hasn't been confirmed yet,

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.310
but it seems very likely
that he will.

